# Copy to .env, or let ./setup-signing.sh write it for you.
#
# None of this is secret. The only real secret in the release path is the
# app-specific notary password, and that lives in the keychain — put there
# once by setup-signing.sh and read back by notarytool, never by these
# scripts. Nothing here is worth protecting beyond keeping .env untracked.
#
# Every value is optional. release.py auto-detects the signing identity when
# exactly one Developer ID Application certificate is installed, and falls
# back to the default profile name. .env is for the machine where that guess
# would be wrong or ambiguous.

# Copy verbatim from: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# Required only when the keychain holds more than one such certificate.
#DEVELOPER_ID="Developer ID Application: Your Name (TEAMID)"

# The Apple ID that holds the Developer Program membership. Used by
# setup-signing.sh only; release.py reads the stored profile instead.
#APPLE_ID="you@example.com"

# Name of the keychain profile created by:
#   xcrun notarytool store-credentials <name> --apple-id ... --team-id ...
#NOTARY_PROFILE="tokens-on-track-notary"
